  "caption": "Quinn thought daily walks had bone health sorted. Then the GP brought up bone health, and Quinn decided to never lift anything again — not even the shopping.\n\nKay explained it's usually the opposite: bone responds to load. Progressive resistance training plus some impact and balance work can help build bone and lower the risk of falls, while walking alone is usually too light.\n\nWhat can help: supervised, progressive strength training, controlled impact scaled to you, and regular balance practice. Strength can improve within weeks, while bone changes take months.\n\nIf you've had a spinal fracture or have several risk factors, loading should be carefully planned and tailored to you.\n\nOur Sydney CBD and Chatswood physios can help. Book via the link in bio.\n\nGeneral information only — not a substitute for an individual assessment.",
